    "notes": "1. The 'total_revenue' field is mapped from the sum of 'Sales and other operating revenue', 'Income from equity affiliates', and 'Other income' as presented in the 'Revenues and other income' section of the statement.\n2. The 'total_operating_cost' field is constructed from all cost items listed under 'Costs and other deductions' except for 'Interest expense' and 'Other taxes and duties'. This includes: Crude oil and product purchases, Production and manufacturing expenses, Selling, general and administrative expenses, Depreciation and depletion (includes impairments), Exploration expenses, and Non-service pension and postretirement benefit expense. This follows standard practice for an integrated oil & gas company where operating costs include cost of goods sold (purchases), production, SG&A, depreciation, and exploration.\n3. 'Other taxes and duties' (26,288 in 2024) is excluded from 'total_operating_cost' as it is considered a non-income-based tax (e.g., property, severance, excise taxes) and is reported separately in the income statement before income tax expense. It is not mapped to any field in the requested schema.\n4. 'Net income' is mapped to 'Net income (loss) attributable to ExxonMobil'.\n5. 'Taxes' is mapped to 'Income tax expense (benefit)'.\n6. 'Interest expenses' is mapped directly.\n7. Supplementary tables provide detailed breakdowns (e.g., components of Other income, equity affiliate details, tax reconciliation, segment data) but do not alter the primary income statement line items used for mapping. Reserve tables are not directly mappable to income statement fields.",
